explanation_preds:
In the context of clock gating, the setup time is the amount of time before the active edge of the clock that the input must be stable to ensure proper operation. The hold time is the amount of time after the active edge of the clock that the input must remain stable. In SDC, these constraints can be represented as follows:
setup: g1 -> clk_A : 50 ps; 
hold: g1 -> clk_A : -20 ps; 
where 50 ps is the setup time and -20 ps is the hold time for the clock signal clk_A. The output clk_out would then be gated based on the state of the input A.

